## Appendix A: Algebraic Derivation of the Coupled Energy-Momentum Equations

Coupling equations (4) and (5):
$$
\begin{cases}
\left(v - \dfrac{c_s^2}{v}\right)\dfrac{dv}{dr} + \dfrac{c_s^2}{T}\dfrac{dT}{dr} = R_1, \\[10pt]
v\dfrac{dv}{dr} + \dfrac{5}{2}\dfrac{c_s^2}{T}\dfrac{dT}{dr} = R_2,
\end{cases}
$$
where
$$
R_1 = \frac{2c_s^2}{r} - \frac{GM_\odot}{r^2} - \frac{1}{\rho}\frac{d}{dr}\!\left(\frac{B^2}{2\mu_0}\right) + \frac{F_{\text{ext}}}{\rho},
$$
$$
R_2 = \frac{Q - \nabla\!\cdot\!\vec{q} - L_{\text{rad}}}{\rho v} + \frac{F_{\text{ext}}}{\rho} - \frac{1}{\rho}\frac{d}{dr}\!\left(\frac{B^2}{2\mu_0}\right) - \frac{GM_\odot}{r^2}.
$$

Solving this linear system yields the temperature gradient expression:
$$
\frac{dT}{dr} = \frac{T}{c_s^2}\,
\frac{ \left(v - \dfrac{c_s^2}{v}\right) R_2 - v R_1 }
{ \dfrac{5}{2}\left(v - \dfrac{c_s^2}{v}\right) - v }.
$$

At the sonic point $v = c_s$, the denominator is $-c_s$, giving $dT/dr|_{r_c} = \frac{T}{c_s^2} R_1|_{r_c}$. Order-of-magnitude analysis requires $R_1(r_c) = 0$, and thus $dT/dr|_{r_c} = 0$.

---

## Appendix B: Parameter Sensitivity Scan — Threshold for Separation of Sonic Point and Temperature Extremum

A systematic scan was performed over four key parameters: effective gravity strength, radiation pressure amplitude, heating scale length, and magnetic pressure gradient. Only when the radial decay scale length of the momentum external force $F_{\text{ext}}$ is $> 5\,R_\odot$ does the separation between $r_c$ and $r_T$ exceed $0.5\,R_\odot$. For the real solar corona, the scale lengths of all momentum terms are $\leq 3\,R_\odot$, so the coincidence condition is robust.

---

## Appendix C: Numerical Methods and Error Tracing

-   **Discretization scheme**: Geometric series grid refinement, convergence criterion of relative residual $<10^{-6}$.
-   **Systematic error breakdown**: 1D spherical symmetry $\sim 7\%$, single-fluid $\sim 5\%$, cooling interpolation $<3\%$, total upper limit $\sim 15\%$.
